    {
      "title": "Find the chance of starting again",
      "body": "<p>A second round happens only if A, B and C all fail in the first round. Find that probability.</p>",
      "recap": "A full losing round brings the game back to the same starting position.",
      "pitfall": "Use each player’s own failure condition.",
      "pause": "Write B’s winning probabilities for the first three rounds and look for a geometric series.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "Write the first few terms of a geometric series to identify its common ratio."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sum all the rounds",
      "body": "<p>Identify the first term and the multiplier between consecutive round probabilities. Check that the multiplier has size less than 1, then use the sum-to-infinity formula.</p>",
      "recap": "A geometric series sums to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pitfall": "B winning in different rounds are separate possible events; add their probabilities.",
      "pause": "Calculate and simplify the total probability.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "A geometric series sums to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> In the first round, B wins exactly when A first fails and B then succeeds. This probability is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math>. C has not yet thrown, so no C factor belongs to this event.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> A full round ends without a winner with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math>. Independent throws mean each further completed losing round multiplies B’s eventual winning contribution by q.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The desired probability is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></math>. The ratio is between 0 and 1, so the series converges. Answer C.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> Equivalently, if p is B’s probability from the start of a round, restarting after a full losing round gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></math>, with the same answer.</p>"
